    "checked_against_source": true,
    "note": "The tables were read from the text layer of the PDF, each value assigned to its column by its position on the page; Appendix D runs down the left column of p. 120 and on into its right one, beside the references, and the two were read apart. In Appendix B a target Al/Si marked * is a sample hydrated for 364 days and ** for 546 days, the others for 182 days; a Ca/Si printed as a lower bound ('≥0.67', amorphous silica present) is kept as that bound with the qualifier 'lower_bound'; a dash in the columns of the other solids (not observed) is written 0, 'trace' is null; 'nd' (no well-defined basal peak) and a dash in the basal spacing are null, and the spacings marked + were measured with anatase as an internal standard ('anatase'), the others without ('external'). The Al/Si of the C-S-H includes the octahedral aluminum the authors assign to the third aluminate hydrate (TAH). In Appendix D a value printed as an upper bound ('≤0.0037') is kept as that bound with the qualifier 'below_detection_limit', a dash (no aluminum in the sample) is left out. Two times are printed 356 days where the others are 364; they are kept as printed."
  },
